  - reverse-engineering
  - android-security
  - firmware-analysis
  - memory-safety
  - differential-testing
abstract: >-
  Type-Driven Binary Auditing via #![forbid(unsafe_code)] Safe Rust Reconstruction uses the
  Rust compiler's strict type, bounds, lifetime, and concurrency rules as a static and
  differential vulnerability discovery oracle against stripped aarch64 binaries. Across 11
  native hardware, imaging, sensor, and biometric subsystems (23 ELF64 binaries, 33 kernels,
  331,853 SplitMix64 and boundary FFI test vectors), this methodology uncovered 20 deterministic
  C/C++ implementation and memory-safety defects (SAM-BUG-01 through SAM-BUG-20) and tracked
  their cross-generation ELF BuildID and .dynsym persistence from Android 10 (SM-G960U) into
  2026 Android 16 flagships (SM-S938B and SM-S948B). Includes the companion #![forbid(unsafe_code)]
  Safe Rust crate s9_camera_gyroscope.
